<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Adwa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1896">1896</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Adwa · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-italo-ethiopian-war">First Italo-Ethiopian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Adwa was fought in 1896 in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> between the forces of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menelik-ii">Menelik II</a> and an invading Italian army. The Ethiopians won a decisive victory, forcing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> to recognise Ethiopian independence. It was a major setback for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a> and became a symbol of African resistance to colonialism.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-adwa.jpg" alt="Battle of Adwa" width="320" height="150" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Franko Khoury. · PDM-owner · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Adwa.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The military zenith came on 1 March 1896, when Menelik II's army of approximately 100,000 routed General Baratieri's Italian force at <b>Adwa</b>, killing over 6,000 Italian and colonial troops and capturing some 3,000 more.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Expansion soon collided with the independent Ethiopian Empire, culminating in the disastrous defeat at <b>Adwa</b> in 1896, where Emperor Menelik II routed the army of General Oreste Baratieri.</blockquote><a href="/empire/italian-empire">Italian Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Colonial expansion followed, with Eritrea organised as a colony in 1890 and a protectorate over much of Somalia, but the attempt to conquer Ethiopia ended in defeat at the <b>Battle of Adwa</b> in 1896.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Ethiopia’s victory over an Italian army at <b>Adwa</b> in 1896 made it a symbol of African freedom for Black people everywhere.</blockquote><a href="/movement/pan-africanism">Pan-Africanism · Background</a></li><li><blockquote>An early line recalling the Italian defeat at <b>Adwa</b> in 1896, which the regime did not want brought to mind, was replaced by a more general one.</blockquote><a href="/songs/faccetta-nera">Faccetta nera</a></li><li><blockquote>It became the base for Italian ambitions in the Horn of Africa, checked at <b>Adwa</b> in 1896.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/january-1">1 January in history</a></li></ul></section>
